Recommends: gnome-settings-daemon
Conflicts: dell-display-manager
Replaces: dell-display-manager
Description: switch inputs, Picture-by-Picture and KVM on Dell monitors
 A GTK 4 / libadwaita application and command line tool that controls Dell
 monitors over DDC/CI, providing on GNOME what Dell Display and Peripheral
 Manager provides on macOS and Windows:
 .
  * select the active video input
  * turn Picture-by-Picture on or off, swap sides, choose the right input
  * hand the monitor's built-in KVM (USB hub with keyboard and mouse)
    to the other computer
  * optional system-wide GNOME keyboard shortcuts for all of the above
 .
 Developed and tested on the Dell U4025QW; vendor VCP codes are
 configurable for other models.
